# Scratch output from `capture.mjs` when run without an output directory: it defaults to
# `shots/` in the working directory, which is the repo root.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash, and that matters. Unanchored, `shots/` matches a `shots`
# directory at *any* depth - including `tools/shots/`, the harnesses themselves. The four
# that existed when this rule was written survived only because git ignores nothing it is
# already tracking; every harness added afterwards was silently dropped, and `bingo.mjs`
# was documented in the README for a whole release without ever being in the repo.
/shots/
